    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the **no-future-date** rule for `POST /api/owners`: a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date is now rejected with **400**.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern used throughout the project (mirroring the existing `ValidatePostcode` \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` flow), I added:\n\n1. **`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a validation step reading `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`. `registrationDate` is optional, so a `null` value passes; a supplied date after `LocalDate.now()` throws the checked `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 the checked exception.\n\n3. **`FutureRegistrationDateHandler`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 responds `400 BAD_REQUEST` with the message.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted the `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` step into `owners.POST.yml` right after `validate` (which publishes the body as a variable) and before `validatePostcode`, so the future-date check runs early and rejects before any persistence work.\n\nThe step is placed after `RequireOwnerFields` (which republishes the body via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`) so it can consume it with `@Val`, consistent with the other validation steps.",
